// M4: an all-zero excitation is a zero right-hand side. The CG convergence test is
// res < max(rel_tol * 0, abs_tol) = 0, which fails, and the solver produces 0/0 = NaN
// ("did NOT converge ... nan"). With the sweep off there are no other states, so the
// skipped excitation also fails the run (M3: exit nonzero).
{
  "Problem":
  {
    "Type": "Magnetostatic",
    "Verbose": 2,
    "Output": "postpro/out_m4"
  },
  "Model":
  {
